license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-29"
keywords:
  - allostery
  - cheminformatics
  - machine-learning
  - drug-discovery
  - ChEMBL
  - benchmark
  - dataset-bias
abstract: >
  A reproducible benchmark asking whether ligand structure alone can separate
  allosteric from orthosteric modulators. Labels are derived from ChEMBL assay
  descriptions with audited, unit-tested text rules; the dataset uses a
  matched-target design in which every retained target carries compounds of
  both classes. Models are evaluated under random, scaffold-out, temporal and
  target-out cross-validation, against a target-identity-only confound probe
  and a physicochemical-property baseline, with class-stratified and paired
  bootstrap confidence intervals and a label-permutation null control.
